comments.body:
@eellison , @xmfan , @mlazos , The RCA is that there is not synchronize_event supported in inductor and dynamo is calling call_method instead of call _function on even synchronization . This will result in race condition to sync host and device. I think we can support synchornize_event in inductor lowering by: 

`make_fallback(torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event.default)`

 and add custom ops in  dynamo streams:

`@custom_op("streams::synchronize_event", mutates_args=())
def synchronize_event(event_index: int) -> None:
    event = _get_event_by_index(event_index)
    event.synchronize()


@synchronize_event.register_fake
def _(
    event_index: int,
) -> None:
    pass


has_side_effect(torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event.default)`

In EventVariableTracker support that using: 

```
        elif name == "synchronize":
            tx.output.create_proxy(
                "call_function", torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event,
                (self.user_object_index,),
                {},
            )
```
This adds sync in events. Please let me know your opinion and the I can create PR for the same.

